<h2>Indian rice and grains for export</h2>
<p>Rice is the centrepiece of this category and the product where India's global position is strongest — the country supplies roughly 80% of the world's traded basmati. Beyond basmati, we handle parboiled non-basmati, maize, wheat and the millet group (jowar, bajra, ragi), all sortex-cleaned and packed to your specification.</p>

<h2>Export policy matters enormously in this category</h2>
<p>More than any other category we handle, grains are subject to active Indian government export management. As things stand, non-basmati white rice remains prohibited for export — a restriction in place since 2023. Parboiled rice is permitted but has carried an export duty. Wheat has swung between prohibition and free export more than once.</p>
<p>We track this continuously, and we'd rather tell you a product isn't currently exportable than take an order we can't lawfully fulfil. When you enquire, we confirm the current position for your specific product before quoting.</p>

<h2>Specifying rice properly</h2>
<p>Rice quotes are only comparable when the specification matches. The parameters that matter:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Variety</strong> — 1121, Pusa 1509/1401, traditional basmati, or the specific non-basmati type.</li>
  <li><strong>Processing</strong> — raw, steam, sella (parboiled) or golden sella. These are different products.</li>
  <li><strong>Average grain length</strong> in mm, before cooking.</li>
  <li><strong>Broken percentage</strong> — 1%, 2%, 5%.</li>
  <li><strong>Moisture</strong> — ≤12–13%.</li>
  <li><strong>Purity</strong> — percentage of the stated variety in the lot.</li>
  <li><strong>Aging</strong> — 12 or 24 months, where relevant.</li>
</ul>
<p>Our <a href="/products/grains-rice/basmati-rice/">basmati rice page</a> goes through each of these in detail.</p>

<h2>Packing and loading</h2>
<p>Standard export packing is 5kg to 50kg PP, BOPP or jute bags, with non-woven and cloth bags available and private-label retail packs supported for branded programmes. Grain loading is weight-limited — around 24–26 MT in a 20ft — so the container fills by weight well before it fills by volume. Use our <a href="/resources/container-loading-calculator/">container loading calculator</a> for a planning estimate.</p>

